{
  "id": "2026-10-03-aiplatform-v1beta1",
  "date": "2026-10-03",
  "api": "aiplatform.v1beta1",
  "service": "Vertex AI",
  "title": "Vertex AI: Custom Voices, Breaking Changes, and a Rollback",
  "summary": "Vertex AI introduces a new API for managing custom voices, enabling creation, retrieval, and deletion. This update also brings several breaking changes, including new read-only fields and type changes for `structuredPrompt`. Notably, some `A2ATaskRecord` fields previously made read-only have been reverted.",
  "details": "Developers can now manage custom voices via the new `projects.locations.voices` resource, with methods like `create`, `delete`, `get`, and `list`. This enables creating prompted or replicated voices and listing both custom and prebuilt options with various filters. Additionally, the `projects.updateCacheConfig` method now supports an `updateMask` parameter for granular control over cache settings.\n\nThis update includes several breaking changes: the `parent` and `name` parameters are now strictly required for the new `voices` methods. Several properties in `GenaiVertexV1beta1Voice` (`expireTime`, `id`, `key`, `sampleAudio`, `usage`) and `GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1TuningJob` (`gcsMetricsUri`) are now read-only. Furthermore, the `structuredPrompt` property in `CloudAiLargeModelsVisionExperimentsResponseProEditResult` and `CloudAiLargeModelsVisionGenerateVideoExperimentsProEditConfig` has changed type from `object` to `string`; update your code if you're using these experimental video features.\n\nIn a notable rollback, `status` in `GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1A2ATaskRecord` and `message`, `state` in `GoogleCloudAiplatformV1beta1A2ATaskRecordStatus` are no longer read-only, reverting a previous breaking change. Agent methods now primarily recommend the `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/aiplatform` scope, though `cloud-platform` remains supported.",
  "impact": "high",
  "breaking": true,
  "interesting_score": 9,
  "tags": [
    "AI/ML",
    "Vertex AI",
    "Breaking Change",
    "New Feature",
    "Voice AI"
  ],
